{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits","id":1513911,"title":"Have you/your players ever used disciplines/sorcery for scholarly pursuits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-04T20:07:44-07:00","id":1513911,"title":"Have you/your players ever used disciplines/sorcery for scholarly pursuits?","content":"Like using dominate/auspex to study the mind, using vicissitude to see how the human body will react to a slightly altered organ, or even using sorcery to try codifying the spiritual?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T22:59:49-07:00","id":1513914,"title":"","content":"Had a PC in a game that had Dominate and would do masquerade clean up work. Every now and then they would come across a mortal who needed a mind wipe, if they annoyed the PC in addition to altering their memories, the PC would implant suggestions to see if they could get around the Dominate rule of killing yourself or inducing self-harm.<br /> <br /> The technique they settled on was to implant a suggestion that every time the mortal was about to climax, they had to think of something horrible/mood killing which prevented them from ever getting off regardless how hard they try. Since the thing they had to think about wasn't fixed, the target never got desensitized to the mechanism. This is the nightmare version of a serial killers warped sexual needs mixed with phantom limb syndrome where you can't scratch an itch because the limb is gone, but still constantly feel it.<br /> <br /> In about 6 - 8 months the mortal usually either committed suicide or died in some extreme sex act meant to try to beat the mental block. We referred to the technique as &quot;over edging&quot; a mortal. Through this and other experiments the character amassed quite the library of Dominate techniques and concepts to use. In addition to earning Boons for Masquerade clean ups, there was also the offer to teach neonates better ways to use Dominate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T00:02:50-07:00","id":1513921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1513914#post1513914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dominate rule of killing yourself or inducing self-harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was always a bit interesting - and oh boy, players are creative when it comes to dominate!<br /> Then when this happened in Beckett's Jyhad Diary?<br /> <br /> <b>Man\u2019s voice: </b>I\u2019m not going home with an incomplete set because some spoiled brat with inheritance took a shine to the pretty picture. Do you know who I am?\u200b<br /> <b>Nicolai: </b>Please do me the kindness of forgetting how to breathe.<br /> [CHOKING SOUNDS]<br /> <b>Beckett:</b> Is he...? Did you just...?<br /> <b>Nicolai: </b>No. The body\u2019s involuntary functions are not so easily controlled. When he loses consciousness, he will begin breathing again. But my control is strong. He will likely wake up and forget again, and again, and again.<br /> [CONTINUED CHOKING]\u200b<br /> ...<br /> [SOUND OF A BODY COLLAPSING]<br /> <br /> <br /> Boy, Hell broke loose and they got new ideas... not that they needed any, but an example enough to spark new creativity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T03:39:58-07:00","id":1513929,"title":"","content":"At some point during a years long chronicle, my group has decided their <i>true </i>goal is cracking the interactions between quantum mechanics and the mystic properties of the universe (basically what House Skopos in Mage does). They set up a full laboratory with enchanted instruments to test theories, leaving me as ST to juggle metaphysics against real world physics and deciding just how much information morsels I can hand out before reality collapses in some unholy paradox. It can be difficult to manage, but on the other hand their 'research' forces me to figure out some fundamental WOD stuff, which is fun.<br /> <br /> I'm still tempted to just send a nexus crawler at times, though.<br /> <br /> On the vampire side of things I had a Tremere player doing some really nasty stuff with vitae refinement and looking into the whole Curse and Blood Potency shtick. He was more or less convinced that generations were some arbitrary numbers assigned 'from the bottom up', and there was no 1st gen progenitor.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wow, I completely missed to mention the powers they use(d).<br /> <br /> The Tremere's study mostly revolved around <i>Blood of Potency</i>. If you can magically lower the generation of your own vitae, it should be possible to do it in other ways than with a Path and more permanently. He also dabbled in Alchemy, trying to refine vitae by separating the potent from the mundane components. Rituals like <i>Blood Walk</i> also featured in the research. Dealing with the necessary vessels for his experiments got very messy.<br /> <br /> My current group is cross-splat and uses a mix of powers. The initial research involved an Ananasi peeking into the Umbra at the Pattern Web while performing a Gift power, and note down the interactions. The Oneiromancer is doing similar things with dream-stuff, and is currently busy trying to overlap dream-spaces and material spaces with a Ritual.<br /> The group's focus at the moment is on trying to determine a relationship between the Pattern Web and quantum foam/vacuum potential, and to this end set up measuring devices that pick up local variations in the Casimir force. Mundane physics, but they used some Technomancy to help with the function of the devices, as well as meta-magic (Quintessence Manipulation) to direct magic juice to the right places.<br /> There's probably some Auspex/Thauma combos that could be used to similar effects if a Vampire were involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 06-05-2023, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T06:32:37-07:00","id":1513946,"title":"","content":"Their was a cappadocian/harbinger npc who used necromancy to reconstruct Byzantine history. He'd interrogate Wraiths and spectre from the period and try and aquire relics. Then every couple of years he'd leak some of the lore to academia in a plausable context.<br /> <br /> Their was also an antiduluvian who didn't produce a clan who used auspex to monitor sociological an scientific developments as her subject of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T09:55:37-07:00","id":1513958,"title":"","content":"I'd argue the overwhelming majority of Thaumaturgy and Vicissitude is done with scholarly intent. Necromancy is maybe 1/3 scholarly (half of it is about socializing with ghosts, and a little bit of it is about necrophilia, but the rest is scholarly stuff, Honest!') <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T12:40:27-07:00","id":1513965,"title":"","content":"My own Thaumaturges always seem to be primarily motivated by money, dear boy (well, boons. Power, influence.) Knowledge is the stepping stone to ruling the city while living in the lap of luxury. <br /> The second goal of research for my Thaumaturges, going hand in hand with profit, is innovation. Quality of life improvements. Research continues into rituals and paths for better herds, circumvention of reliance on human society, safer acquisition of blood, circumvention of vampiric weaknesses, longer periods of activity and daywalking, better personal security, a stronger Masquerade, improvement of Technomancy and that newfangled vampire internet the neonates are raving about these nights...<br /> <br /> So, for example, setting up test sites for experiments with the Path of Conjuring for mass manufacturing, and Neptune and the Levinbolt for producing indoor plumbing and running electricity without needing to touch the grid or needing to fiddle around with paperwork and bills.<br /> <br /> And tying into this; vicissitude. Can one mess around with the human brain to create a mindless, docile lump of flesh that still produces quality blood without the pesky nonsense of sapience and risk of discovery?<br /> Can we improve the kine in our herds? Make them produce more blood? Either yielding greater quantities, or simply recovering it at greater speeds to enable more frequent feedings and less potential complications for the blood bag.<br /> How much mastery of the discipline does it take to make these changes genetic?<br /> <br /> (And also sometimes I just to see what happens if, say, you alter two strangers to look like each other and what chaos results. Do they assume the other is some kind of shapeshifting monster that has stolen their life? Should I plant this ide for them?)<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> Same goes for dominate: what kind of psychological experiments can I perform today? For example, if I rip out your entire life and rewrite it, who are you? What's the viability of conditioning the next generation of kine en masse in their nursery classes? What are the side effects of such overuse?<br /> Can dominate be used to condition someone to be more susceptible to other kind affecting disciplines like obfuscate?<br /> <br /> And then other characters push the limits of their disciplines for similar pragmatic purposes. For example, ways to utilise obfuscate, chimestry and presence's effects to hide kindred society in plain sight.<br /> <br /> My Necromancers usually go scholarly-ish.<br /> <br /> Got one who lets wraiths use him for skinriding in exchange for experiencing their skills, knowledge and memories (especially their death). He's also kind of obsessed with exploring the Underworld with a specific focus on Oblivion and what the hell is wrong with it and the world - hence the fixation on living through the minds of others and exploring outside the bounds of mundane reality. Currently he's trying to crack the rest of the umbra, which he's recently learnt exists. Sometimes likes to eavesdrop at the Fountain of Caroline.<br /> <br /> Another basically lives in the Library of Alexandria down in Stygia, spends most of her time reading the lost works of mankind and only comes back to the Skinlands for feeding and &quot;chores&quot; the Elders want her to do.<br /> <br /> A third, always curious about how vampires are so difficult to distinguish from wraiths in the Underworld, discovered the _ while dealing with a hunter problem. Learning that the undead are indistinguishable from the Restless according to the machine turned curiosity into an obsession. His new project is studying the overlap and differences in Wraiths, Risen and Vampires. For this purpose he's also planning on researching Thaumaturgy and Dur-An-Ki to better understand the properties of the Blood.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T12:46:10-07:00","id":1513966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , discovered the _ while dealing with a hunter problem. </div> </div> </div>&quot;...discovered the SAD's &quot;chaoscopic scanners&quot;...&quot;<br /> <br /> No idea what happened there, but I don't feel safe editing it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T20:10:11-07:00","id":1513984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1513965#post1513965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And tying into this; vicissitude. Can one mess around with the human brain to create a mindless, docile lump of flesh that still produces quality blood without the pesky nonsense of sapience and risk of discovery?<br /> Can we improve the kine in our herds? Make them produce more blood? Either yielding greater quantities, or simply recovering it at greater speeds to enable more frequent feedings and less potential complications for the blood bag.<br /> How much mastery of the discipline does it take to make these changes genetic?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO, pre revised Biothaumathurgy would probably be more useful the vicissitude when dealing with genetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 06-05-2023, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-05T23:28:45-07:00","id":1513988,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy is great at making money, but that's far more due to it's exclusivity and a few high value rituals rather than something that could ever be mass market. Offering the right warding circle to a vampire fearing his life? Give me all your life is worth. Establishing an unbreakable contract? I want a cut. But conjuring valuables en mass? That's just crass. First they're magical items with several things wrong with them waiting to be discovered and that's a masquerade risk, secondly conjured items can't change states so gold or explosives aren't great, if they're pushed too hard they turn into goop. Third: the other spells make so much and mundane businesses are an easier investment. Lastly, the Tremere don't have a great reputation you don't want to make it even worse. <br /> <br /> With this in mind, Tremere business is low volume, crazy margins kind of stuff. That and, like a tech company, the cost of making $$$ after all the RND is done is next to nothing. A Ventrue usually has to give something big up for a deal, the Tremere give up 5-25 minutes of their time typically. As no Tremere needs to spend much time making bank, the time available for scholarly pursuits is huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T00:59:22-07:00","id":1513993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1513988#post1513988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But conjuring valuables en mass? That's just crass. First they're magical items with several things wrong with them waiting to be discovered and that's a masquerade risk, secondly conjured items can't change states so gold or explosives aren't great, if they're pushed too hard they turn into goop. Third: the other spells make so much and mundane businesses are an easier investment. Lastly, the Tremere don't have a great reputation you don't want to make it even worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more of conjuring the likes of furniture, circuit boards, infrastructure and wiring in goal of some kind of &quot;vampire utopia&quot; hidden and detached from mortal society where vampires just produce, sell and install their own stuff to each other while leaving minimum (if any) traces in the human world - definitely not something meant for humans to know of or access - but yeah, there's a reason I said &quot;experiments&quot; and &quot;test site&quot;. Technically the question didn't propose that these characters<i> succeeded </i>in their endeavors or that they were sensible, just asked if they'd played around with their disciplines.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd probably trust the Ventrue and Toreador with running secret kindred-specific businesses rather than letting the Tremere try to play god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T01:14:39-07:00","id":1513994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1513958#post1513958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue the overwhelming majority of Thaumaturgy and Vicissitude is done with scholarly intent. Necromancy is maybe 1/3 scholarly (half of it is about socializing with ghosts, and a little bit of it is about necrophilia, but the rest is scholarly stuff, Honest!')</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Mortis paths are quire overtly scholarly in origin, as a side I suspect modern necromancy/mortis/obliviob is slightly stunted due to the giovannis narrow subject of interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T01:27:56-07:00","id":1513995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1513994#post1513994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Mortis paths are quire overtly scholarly in origin, as a side I suspect modern necromancy/mortis/obliviob is slightly stunted due to the giovannis narrow subject of interest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni, maybe, but some of the other families are still innovating. The Pisanob retain(ed) their Cappadocian elders (before the Harbingers came home with a grudge), and they and the Ghiberti both pioneered new rituals and a path together; and the della Passaglia rather worryingly love necromancy and research thereof for its own sake. They might be stifled by Venice's leashes, but the scholarly interest is there, and probably even more active post-Reunion.<br /> Then there's whatever the Nagaraja are up to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-06-2023, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T06:08:00-07:00","id":1514004,"title":"","content":"Giovanni indeed are like, overwhelmingly more interested in business. The Tremere see the path of blood as a sort of initiation path and everyone will go on to find their real specialities which each stand well alone, but the starting path for the modern necromancer is really the heavy lifter of the discipline: Half of the other paths are support for the primary path, and the others are bullshit. So dominant is sephulcre that if you made it the only path and converted everything else into rituals so you didn't have to pay xp and could skip to the good stuff the former paths combined would probably still be used less than sephulcre. <br /> With the physical necromancy, Bones 1-3 has some use and that one ability that makes you mortal is pretty neat but virtually everything else is a poor allocation of xp. When the best path is the one you start with, you're not really going to develop a clan culture that values research, especially when the Giovanni devoured the guys who did value research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T13:12:26-07:00","id":1514044,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, there isn't really a dedicated discipline for scholars, is there? You would think the Brujah had it somewhere in their blood, but even the 'True' Brujah do not, despite their character archetypes. I mean, Temporis would certainly be useful for cram sessions, but manipulating time is just useful in general.<br /> <br /> I remember making a custom Thauma Path for my Tremere character that focused on acquiring knowledge; speed-reading, book memory/recall, ignoring language barriers, literally sucking the knowledge out of a book/medium. But it feels to me like those abilities would have a place in several Clans. A necromancy Path centered around 'resurrecting' knowledge could be a cool concept too, especially for Cappadocians and their remnants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T23:12:41-07:00","id":1514079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514044#post1514044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, there isn't really a dedicated discipline for scholars, is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends of your field of interest I think<br /> Mytherceria's <b>Steal the Mind</b> (Remove memories and knowledge from a victim temporarily) certanly could help, like <b>Absorb the Mind</b> (Permanently take Ability ranks from a victim for yourself)<br /> Auspex, too with <b>The Spirit's Touch </b>(Learn something of an object and its previous owner from its resonance) and <b>Spirit Ties (</b>Learn something about a target from residues of its tissue); <b>Cipher </b>gives he ability to read any non-supernatural language or code<br /> Dementation's <b>Eyes of Chaos</b> gives insight into the nature of something through seemingly random patterns (and <b>Deny </b>(Ignore the existence of an object and not be affected by it) simply kicks logic and reality in the kiwis...)<br /> Obeah's <b>Auguring the Sickness </b>(Discover the symptoms and severity of an illness in someone) or Valeren's <b>Sense Cycle </b>(Watcher - Sense the cycle of life entire, instinctively knowing when an individual or an event is important to your future), <b>Auguring the Sickness</b>: (Healer - Discover the severity and nature of a sickness plaguing a target) or even <b>Anesthetic Touch/Gift of Sleep</b>: (Healer/Warrior - Remove feelings of pain from a target or put a living creature to sleep) is a must to a doctor<br /> Temporis's <b>Rewind</b> (Observe past events that happened in the area you are standing in) and <b>Clio's Kiss </b>(Bring something or someone from the past into the present) both are crazy usefull<br /> Necromancy's <b>Lifeless Tongues </b>( allows you to speak with the dead in any language) have potenital, not to mention the ritual, <b>Grasp the Ghostly </b>(By chanting for six hours and sacrificing an object roughly equal to its mass, the Necromancer can bring a Relic across the Shroud.)<br /> The Abyss Mysticism's rituals <b>Whispers in the Dark </b>(Fall into torpor and learn hidden secrets from the void) and <b>Commune with the Abyss </b>(Fall into a torpor-like sleep and ask the Abyss a question) technically are the same (I <i>think </i>only version differences there) but from a scholar's point of view... yes, would sell their soul to have answers I think<br /> Speaking of witch, Dark Thaumaturgy's Path of the Unspoken first fouw level are scholar galore:<br /> <b>Whispers of the Unborn</b>: Listen to the forces of entropy to gain the answer to one specific question\u200b<br /> <b>Scribing the Unknown</b>: Transcribe any written information\u200b<br /> <b>Shadow Thoughts</b>: Learn more about a target by conversing with their shadow\u200b<br /> <b>Fragments of the Forgotten</b>: Transcribe information from lost works (missing passages are often filled in with misleading informations)\u200b<br /> Video Nefas (Path of Evil Revelations) could be usefull too while Rego Calatio (Path of Summoning) well summons Demons and Demons are the wellspring of knowledge and informatrion... for a <i>Price</i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-06T23:49:19-07:00","id":1514084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514044#post1514044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, there isn't really a dedicated discipline for scholars, is there? You would think the Brujah had it somewhere in their blood, but even the 'True' Brujah do not, despite their character archetypes. I mean, Temporis would certainly be useful for cram sessions, but manipulating time is just useful in general.<br /> <br /> I remember making a custom Thauma Path for my Tremere character that focused on acquiring knowledge; speed-reading, book memory/recall, ignoring language barriers, literally sucking the knowledge out of a book/medium. But it feels to me like those abilities would have a place in several Clans. A necromancy Path centered around 'resurrecting' knowledge could be a cool concept too, especially for Cappadocians and their remnants.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably deliberate, disciplines are by nature extensions of a vampires predatory nature. Blood magics are tainted and inevitably slants towards destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-07T04:03:21-07:00","id":1514103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514079#post1514079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there are bits and bops scattered throughout the Disciplines, but nothing fully dedicated. Somehow it's incredibly funny to me that the closest thing is a Dark Thauma Path. I need to take a look at Combo Disciplines, especially Auspex + X. I could imagine there could be something useful there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514084#post1514084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably deliberate, disciplines are by nature extensions of a vampires predatory nature. Blood magics are tainted and inevitably slants towards destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Could be, although my guess would be that they put scholars with character archetypes (fighter, mage, thief) and kept the Disciplines for more general use. There are certainly ways to make a scholar predatory and reflect that in a power- the Dark Thauma Path of the Unspoken <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> mentioned is a good example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T04:26:24-07:00","id":1514182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514044#post1514044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, there isn't really a dedicated discipline for scholars, is there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Path of Blood, Path of the Focused Mind, and Auspex do come close in regard to being useful - possibly with some etra and additional capabilities and powers - for a knowledge seeker or a scholar.<br /> <br /> From time to time there are organizations, guilds, and groups mentioned in VtM and WoD books that might directly help scholars, advisors, and researchers in acquiring additionla appropriate and useful abilities. For example there is the Arcanum, and there are Nosferatu Lore Expers . Gangrel Vampires also can be interested in acquiring and sharing stories or knowledge.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:51:49-07:00","id":1514229,"title":"","content":"If I were going to pick a &quot;scholarly&quot; Discipline, I would probably choose the various types of Blood Sorcery, since they essentially let you convert knowledge into almost infinite possible forms of power, given dedication and time. Auspex is probably the runner up.<br /> <br /> More generally, I feel like most Disciplines focus on making the user a better predator, something better capable of catching prey or confronting other predators, with most other uses deriving from there. Pure scholarship, the pursuit of knowledge for its own sake, doesn't tend to mesh with that.<br /> <br /> Also, I find this question kind of entertaining, because while my limited experience play WoD has been as a Storyteller, I have a hard time imagining playing a character that *wouldn't* use their supernatural powers for scholastic purposes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T02:30:54-07:00","id":1514286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514229#post1514229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I find this question kind of entertaining, because while my limited experience play WoD has been as a Storyteller, I have a hard time imagining playing a character that *wouldn't* use their supernatural powers for scholastic purposes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this happens to most - if not every - character or NPC in Vampire: the Masquerade and World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> The role of an investigator or a scout is often certainly needed and required. The nature , meaning, and direction of plots and objectives in WoD means that often there is distinct comptetition and antagonisms even when it comes to simple investigations or knowledge checking and fact finding. Supernatural persons with key and particular powers or unique mental inclinations or useful mundane skills will surely come ahead and achieve glory and auccess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T16:23:34-07:00","id":1514352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514044#post1514044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A necromancy Path centered around 'resurrecting' knowledge could be a cool concept</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so I went ahead and gave this a try because it seemed like a fun idea. I also wanted to emphasize how the predatory nature of a vampire can combine with a scholar archetype and have a Path reflect that, creating something for an insatiable glutton for knowledge. I tried to balance the 'noble' concept of resurrecting knowledge with destruction and egoism.<br /> The numbers for rolls are obviously not tested and done by gut feeling.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dust Path</b><br /> <br /> Unusual for Necromancers, the practitioners of this Path do not primarily deal with Wraiths, but instead have learned to conjure and condense motes of memory from the Shadowlands. Only those fragments of remembrance that have been swallowed by Oblivion are truly lost and beyond the grasp of the Necromancer.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Gather the Mnesia</b><br /> The Necromancer reaches briefly into the Shadowlands, gathers a pinch of fine, gray dust and pulls it into the Skinlands. This substance is known as Mnesia and is an important catalyst in all further powers of the Path.<br /> Mnesia is what is left of souls, memories, and plasm \u2013 the sediment of the underworld, ground down by eons but not yet consumed by Oblivion. When inhaled, ingested, or rubbed into the skin, it acts like a potent memory enhancing drug with a mild hallucinogenic effect. It is quite addictive to kine, and even kindred need to be careful with its use.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>The player spends a blood point and rolls Wits + Occult against the local Shroud rating. A successful roll nets one dose of Mnesia. When consumed or applied as described above, it lowers the difficulty of mental feats related to memory by 3. This includes recalling suppressed or supernaturally erased memories.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Whole in Death</b><br /> The Necromancer rubs one dose of Mnesia onto a heavily damaged object or corpse, and then ceremonially destroys it completely. This creates a Relic of the object which is summoned into the Skinlands to take the place of the original, in pristine condition. This power is mostly used to restore old books, artifacts, relief inscriptions and the like for study. In the case of a corpse, a gestalt body made of memory remnants is created, which can be questioned.<br /> However, Relics do not last long in the Skinlands and after a while will fade into the underworld. Whatever remains of the destroyed original crumbles to dust in seconds after that.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The player rolls Dexterity + Occult against a difficulty of 7. A success means the object or corpse is restored for one scene, or longer for extra successes. It is possible to extend this duration with repeated use of the power and application of Mnesia when the Relic begins to fade.<br /> Note that corpses reanimated in this manner do not summon a Wraith, but may attract its attention. The gestalt body contains the memories and personality of the living person up to the moment of death, and depending on circumstances may be hostile or uncooperative.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Thirst of Coeus</b><br /> While feeding from a vessel under the influence of Mnesia, the Necromancer can draw out and remove secrets, knowledge, or memories from the victim together with their blood or vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The player must specify the memory they intend to drain. The base difficulty of the Manipulation + Occult roll is 10, but is lowered by one for each previously consumed blood point. The player must decide at which point during the feeding process they want to execute the power. A single success is sufficient to drain the desired memory, but extra successes can increase details or scope. The victim may try to resist with a difficulty 8 Willpower roll, soaking successes.<br /> Characters with the necessary level in the Vitreous Path may use this power on Wraiths after blowing the Mnesia on their Corpus.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Deny the Maw</b><br /> This power allows the Necromancer to capture the soul escaping from a dying body. They sprinkle a dose of Mnesia over the victim, literally pull the soul out, and then warp it into the shape of a physical object.<br /> Most commonly, the shape of a book is chosen, but some prefer musical instruments or another type of object that can \u2018speak\u2019. That is because an item created this way retains the memories of the captured soul, which are reflected in its function. For example, the content of a soul-bound book will contain passages of the victim\u2019s life, texts about their passions, or unrealized ideas. The content may even change over time, or rotate through topics. An instrument will whisper these things when played, while scenes may appear as faded visions on the surface of water in a soul-bound bowl. The power also works on weakened Wraiths, but in order to succeed requires possession of a Fetter item.<br /> The binding is permanent and irreversible. Any Wraith seeing such an object would identify it as a soulforged item and rightfully wonder how it got on the wrong side of the Shroud.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>The player spends a point of Willpower and then rolls a Willpower test against 8. A success means the soul was captured and the player chooses what kind of object they would like to forge from the Corpus of the soul. When attempting the use of this power on a Wraith, the Willpower roll is contested and the character must possess at least one Fetter item of the Wraith.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Gnostic Chains</b><br /> After tossing a dose of Mnesia in the air before them, temporary Fetters bind nearby Wraiths to the Necromancer, creating conduits through which the accumulated knowledge and skills of the ghosts can be channeled. This power can also be used as a means of information gathering, as the bound Wraiths become mere extensions of the Necromancer\u2019s mind. Fast thinking casters have employed this as a lighting rod mechanic to lessen the impact of a mental attack on them, diverting the brunt of the effect onto the ghosts. While bound, the Wraiths become catatonic and all their senses are shut off. If they are attacked, the link to the caster severs.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The player spends a Willpower point and rolls Stamina + Occult against the local Shroud rating. For each success one Wraith is bound to the Necromancer, increasing a Skill, Talent, or Knowledge rating of the player\u2019s choice by one, for one scene. Abilities raised by this power can not exceed the maximum rating set by the generation of the caster, but the same Ability can be raised multiple times.<br /> Additionally, the caster has access to the memories of the bound Wraiths and can search them for useful information. For example, whether they have seen a specific person or witnessed an event in the area. The caster can sacrifice the link to one of the bound Wraiths to divert a single mental attack. If choosing to do so, they must remove one of the temporary Ability increases.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rituals / Mnesia Alchemy</b><br /> <br /> Rituals associated with the Dust Path are alchemical procedures that require an Intelligence + Alchemy roll (difficulty 3 + level of the procedure) to perform, as well as the necessary equipment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Plasmic Guide (Level One)</b><br /> Mixing a point of vitae, ectoplasm, Mnesia, and then incubating it for a month in a hermetically sealed jar, the Necromancer creates a small Plasmic homunculus. It follows them in the Shadowlands and is sensitive to caches of lost knowledge, to which it will draw attention (\u201cHey! Listen!\u201d). It may also alert the caster in case of imminent threats on the far side of the Shroud, or perform simple scouting tasks there. It is otherwise very weak and a single successful attack will destroy it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fickle Memories (Level Two)</b><br /> In an hour long process, the Necromancer crafts an artificial memory which they then imbue together with a bit of their vitae into a dose of Mnesia, which is then calcified. If blown onto a victim, the false memory will be implanted in the target\u2019s mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Blood Remembers (Level Three)</b><br /> Ingesting a distilled and putrefied mixture of vitae or blood and Mnesia, the alchemist receives potent visions of events in the life of the donor, or the donor\u2019s bloodline. Extra successes mean the visions go further back in the line of the donor\u2019s ancestral line, kindred or kine. This elixir is mostly used to uncover secrets of the bloodlines, and can be greatly enhanced if laced with water from the River of Death, granting the Necromancer control over the visions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pasiphae Extract (Level Four)</b><br /> The Necromancer must capture a Wraith and trap it in a container or immobile form. They then put it into the athanor, burning away the Psyche until only the calcified Shadow remains. This is then crushed and mixed with Mnesia, dissolved in water, filtered, and finally distilled. The result is one fluid ounce of pitch black liquid, that if ingested, induces acute dementia in the victim. The effect starts slow but is incremental, and unless the warped Shadow is exorcised, utterly complete.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>From Beyond the Lethe (Level Five)</b><br /> The alchemist mixes five doses of Mnesia, bone meal, and scrapings of a type of lichen that grows on tombstones with blood until they have made a dough. This must be left to rest and rise before it is baked into a small loaf of blood bread. When ingested, the consciousness is projected into the Tempest.<br /> This is an extremely dangerous endeavor, as the Tempest presents a very real danger to the projection. The journey is therefore only made in a last ditch effort to hunt down fragments of a precious secret before they tumble into Oblivion.<br /> The effect lasts one day, during which time the body of the Necromancer appears to be in Torpor.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 06-10-2023, 05:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T16:42:07-07:00","id":1514354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514352#post1514352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Dust Path</b><br /> <br /> Unusual for Necromancers, the practitioners of this Path do not primarily deal with Wraiths, but instead have learned to conjure and condense motes of memory from the Shadowlands. Only those fragments of remembrance that have been swallowed by Oblivion are truly lost and beyond the grasp of the Necromancer.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny how the best necromancy paths tend to be fan made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T02:05:30-07:00","id":1514431,"title":"","content":"Thank you! The level five example ritual got cut off in the original post, so I edited that back in.<br /> <br /> Rituals as alchemy are fun to thought experiment with; I could probably spend days imagining weird recipes with exotic components and what their effect might be.<br /> <br /> Edit: ...aaaand the spam filter ate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 06-10-2023, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T09:44:52-07:00","id":1514472,"title":"","content":"You know outside of my second character who is a Malkavian who poses as a researcher at a investagative agency with his Nosferatu buddy, I never used any of the disciplines for scholarly pursuits and I've only being doing it recently now in our game and gave my Brujah a well earned rest for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T02:31:24-07:00","id":1514811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits?p=1514352#post1514352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dust Path</b><br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks to the admin who unlocked my post.<br /> <br /> I think I will try to formalize the two Thauma paths in the same vein I had made ages ago for a LARP and adapt them to TT.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T17:02:16-07:00","id":1515316,"title":"","content":"<b>Ars Notoria</b><br /> <br /> Practitioners of this Path employ a technique called <i>Method of Loci</i> to improve their memories and general mental capacities. They build a mental space, which represents a vault of knowledge \u2013 a mental library \u2013 which they can enter through meditation. With each advancement on the Path, they expand this memory palace and add more utility.<br /> This technique is much older than its name, and a staple in many magic traditions. As a result, the <i>Ars Notoria</i> can be found in variants throughout all schools of sorcery. Even in cultures without written language, the symbol of the book can be replaced with mnemonic devices to achieve the same effect. Modern versions tend to replace rows of bookshelves with a data center and terminals, but the exact expression depends on the preferences of the practitioner.<br /> <br /> In game terms, the levels of this Path double as ranks in a combined but somewhat limited, specialized version of the <i>Demesne</i> and <i>Library</i> Backgrounds. These benefits are accessible without blood cost, but require a moment of focus to enter the mental space:<br /> <br /> \u2022 The time needed for theoretical research is dramatically reduced. Without restraints of the physical body (or physical laws), things move much faster inside the mind. This can be exploited to use the mental library as an efficient space for research and study.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Having access to memories in a well organized structure results in a type of Eidetic Memory. The Sorcerer is able to recall minute details and examine memories at leisure. One specialized application of this is speed-reading, where having caught a brief glimpse of a page is sufficient to recall and study its contents.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Many practitioners employ tulpas, semi-autonomous thoughtforms that are part of the Sorcerer\u2019s subconsciousness. These can act as librarians and scribes, performing menial tasks of organization and cataloging, while the attention of the Sorcerer is otherwise occupied.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Characters can usually enter their mental library within a single turn and without a roll, if undisturbed. Depending on distractions, a successful Perception + Path Rating roll (difficulty 5 and up) may be necessary. While inside, they are not completely deprived of their sensory connection to the outside world, but may suffer increased difficulty to their Alertness rolls.<br /> <br /> There is no hard rule on the perceived time dilation the Sorcerer experiences, and it should be treated narratively by the Storyteller. If tulpas are employed, the Sorcerer is able to maintain one per Path Rating \u2013 they should be treated more as automatons than conscious agents. They are just symbols for subconscious tasks of categorization, mental sorting, or \u2018ambient\u2019 thoughts on various topics the Sorcerer performs and do not require active attention.<br /> <br /> Like any other Demesne, the library is a space that can be invaded by mental attacks or certain powers. The consequences of an enemy plundering the well organized memories of the character should be obvious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Powers</b><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Librarium</b><br /> The Sorcerer puts their accumulated knowledge to use, mentally collecting references for a task and using them to improve their performance.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The player may allocate temporary bonus dots equal to their Path Rating to Abilities of their choice, as long as they have the necessary sources to draw on in their mental library. The number of successes on the roll to activate the power is the number of turns these dots remain.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Tablinum</b><br /> The Sorcerer is able to transfer the contents of any medium into their mind by touch, or fill a blank medium with contents from their mind. While this is an effective way to quickly transfer information, it can also be used to create convincing forgeries. The medium itself does not change, and during the transfer, an onlooker may notice dim streams of letters flowing along the arm of the Sorcerer.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The transfer time for the contents of an average book is one turn, but may be longer for large volumes of data. The number of successes on the roll to activate the power can be used to determine the volume of data transferred per turn, with about one Gigabyte of information per success. If used to create a forgery, the successes increase the difficulty to identify it as such. The Sorcerer must be able to touch the medium \u2018as an item\u2019: putting their hand on the case of a desktop computer will not work, but a cased external drive would.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Scriptorium</b><br /> Through immersion and observation, the caster is quickly able to adapt to new and foreign concepts by cross-referencing them with their own accumulated knowledge. After spending enough time with something new, they can add it to their library, and learn it at an astounding rate.<br /> This power can be used to quickly pick up new languages, foreign etiquette, new rituals, an obscure branch of mathematics or anything else the Sorcerer did not previously know before.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>After at least one scene of witnessing whatever new knowledge the character wants to acquire, the player may deduct the successes on the roll to activate the power from the XP cost of a corresponding character trait (to a minimum of 1) and immediately purchase it. If the player does not have sufficient XP, they may choose to \u2018sell\u2019 permanent points of Willpower. In case it needs to be said, this power obviously can not pick up traits that are incompatible with the nature of the caster, such as the Gifts of a werewolf or awakened Magick.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Laboratorium</b><br /> The Sorcerer thoughtcrafts a space for experimentation and creation of new knowledge. A mental study or laboratory has many advantages over its mundane counterpart: it is always accessible, any necessary tools can be created by a thought, and the very laws of the realm obey the will of the researcher. While the experiments may not be repeatable in the physical world, the Sorcerers have found a way to circumvent this problem. This power allows them to transfer physical objects between their mental laboratory and the outside. Aside from providing a fantastic creative space, it is also a useful cache for equipment.<br /> <br /> There are, however, some limitations: First, objects with more mass or larger than the caster can not be transferred. Second, no self-aware beings can be transported. Reportedly, there have been successful summonings of ephemeral entities inside a mental laboratory, but most researchers wisely stick to lab mice. Third, anything brought to the outside must consist of physical material \u2013 in other words, built from materials first brought inside. And finally, any object brought outside with too outlandish properties will be subject to Paradox and destroyed.<br /> <br /> <b>System: </b>The number of successes on the roll to activate this power determines the total mass of objects that can be transferred. The exact nature and results of the experiments depends on the nature of research and what the Sorcerer\u2019s goal is and should be handled separately. The Sorcerer can work in the laboratory while physically sleeping.<br /> <br /> <i>Example: Hassam al-Zaher, who researches the properties of the Shroud, wants to test a theory that the emotions of mortals affect the local Shroud strength. He transports canvas, painting colors, and some alchemical components into his mental laboratory. Hassam can create painting utensils and the equipment to alchemically process the colors by will, and crafts some paintings that supernaturally evoke different emotions in a viewer, but also record variations in the Shroud strength on the back of the canvas. Once finished, he can transport the paintings to the outside.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Stellarium</b><br /> By this point, the Demesne has become strong enough to connect with the Astral Umbra, allowing the Sorcerer to project into and explore the very realm of ideas.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> A successful roll to activate this power allows the character to exit their mental library and fully project into the Astral Umbra, usually the Vulgate. The physical body appears to be in torpor, and loses all sensual connection to the physical world.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_b